      "side": 1,
      "message": "From previous experiences, implicit casting \"could\" introduce very-hard-to-debug bug (depends on compiler\u0027s behavior).\n\nWhen casting between: signed vs. unsigned, and different bit lengths, I usually explicit specify them (and cast step by step).\n\n  s8 \u003c---\u003e u8\n   ^        ^\n   |        |\n   v        v\n  s32 \u003c---\u003e u32\n\nIn short: I usually don\u0027t cast \"cross\" the graph (e.g. u8-\u003es32), instead u8-\u003es8-\u003es32.\n\nIn some use cases, UBSAN would complain (e.g. left shift on signed integer).",
      "parentUuid": "0c515b57_e6a9a4ad",
